1
00:00:22,021 --> 00:00:23,857
Oh, there you are!

2
00:00:23,940 --> 00:00:24,858
What?

3
00:00:26,901 --> 00:00:29,070
Jogo!

4
00:00:34,617 --> 00:00:36,995
Seems like your body
is almost completely restored.

5
00:00:37,495 --> 00:00:40,498
Yes, it's comfortable to live here.

6
00:00:40,582 --> 00:00:42,917
No humans can come close.

7
00:00:43,001 --> 00:00:45,879
I guess it's really inconvenient
when you don't have a body.

8
00:00:45,962 --> 00:00:48,631
Self-regeneration
is really inefficient, too.

9
00:00:48,715 --> 00:00:49,883
Mahito.

10
00:00:49,966 --> 00:00:53,178
Seems like you used up
a lot of cursed energy as well.

11
00:00:53,261 --> 00:00:55,138
Oh, you can tell?

12
00:00:55,221 --> 00:00:58,892
Ryomen Sukuna and his vessel
are my nemesis.

13
00:00:59,851 --> 00:01:03,980
This game started when I met my new toy,

14
00:01:04,481 --> 00:01:06,816
but it didn't go well.

15
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:08,359
It wasn't bad at first, though.

16
00:01:08,860 --> 00:01:13,406
I should have taken the toy hostage,
and forced Itadori to make a Binding Vow.

17
00:01:13,490 --> 00:01:18,119
If you don't want him to die,
hand over your body to Sukuna.

18
00:01:19,746 --> 00:01:24,125
No, a Binding Vow
can only be done by himself.

19
00:01:24,209 --> 00:01:28,505
It's not that simple to initiate
a Binding Vow through intervention.

20
00:01:30,715 --> 00:01:32,884
Maybe it would have been better

21
00:01:32,967 --> 00:01:35,762
if I just gave him a fatal blow
instead of transfiguring him.

22
00:01:36,429 --> 00:01:39,557
Maybe Sukuna could have treated him
with his Reverse Cursed Technique.

23
00:01:41,309 --> 00:01:44,896
Know your place, you fool.

24
00:01:46,022 --> 00:01:50,777
No, that's how he is.
He'll refuse no matter what.

25
00:01:52,070 --> 00:01:53,321
Jogo.

26
00:01:54,155 --> 00:01:56,157
After coming in contact with Sukuna,

27
00:01:56,241 --> 00:01:59,327
I think it's better
to follow Geto's plan first.

28
00:01:59,911 --> 00:02:02,705
Sukuna is worth the effort.

29
00:02:05,125 --> 00:02:09,879
Collect all fingers
and offer it to Sukuna?

30
00:02:10,797 --> 00:02:14,551
It doesn't matter
if we all die in the process.

31
00:02:15,468 --> 00:02:16,928
Right?

32
00:02:17,971 --> 00:02:19,472
Very well.

33
00:02:19,556 --> 00:02:23,560
It doesn't have to be me smiling
in the wilderness 100 years later.

34
00:02:23,643 --> 00:02:26,896
I'm fine with it,
as long as curses live as humans.

35
00:02:26,980 --> 00:02:29,399
Oh, you get it.

36
00:02:29,482 --> 00:02:34,028
So let's collect all six fingers
kept by Jujutsu High School.

37
00:02:34,112 --> 00:02:35,363
Is that necessary?

38
00:02:35,864 --> 00:02:39,617
Jujutsu Sorcerers keep Yuji Itadori
because they want him

39
00:02:39,701 --> 00:02:41,369
to swallow Sukuna's fingers, right?

40
00:02:41,452 --> 00:02:43,663
Even if we ignore him,
he'll eat it by himself.

41
00:02:44,247 --> 00:02:45,623
The higher-ups of Jujutsu High

42
00:02:45,707 --> 00:02:49,627
still can't judge
Yuji Itadori's strength as a vessel.

43
00:02:49,711 --> 00:02:52,714
They don't know how many fingers it takes
for him to lose control.

44
00:02:52,797 --> 00:02:56,551
They will probably gather all the fingers
before making him swallow all at once.

45
00:02:57,427 --> 00:02:59,596
Although there's one exception.

46
00:03:00,096 --> 00:03:02,682
I want him to eat it quickly!

47
00:03:02,765 --> 00:03:04,976
We can't wait that long, right?

48
00:03:05,059 --> 00:03:09,397
In a worst-case scenario,
the higher-ups might kill Yuji Itadori.

49
00:03:09,898 --> 00:03:12,442
Nothing ventured, nothing gained.

50
00:03:12,984 --> 00:03:15,111
What should we do?

51
00:03:15,194 --> 00:03:16,863
I've made the arrangements.

52
00:03:17,363 --> 00:03:21,868
That's why I let Jujutsu High School
gather the fingers I collected.

53
00:04:59,966 --> 00:05:05,471
Nanami, tell me something interesting.

54
00:05:06,931 --> 00:05:08,808
All right, I got it!

55
00:05:08,891 --> 00:05:12,353
Let's play catch with scrap rice balls

56
00:05:12,437 --> 00:05:14,564
and discuss secularism!

57
00:05:14,647 --> 00:05:17,108
Then I'll upload a video on it.
It will be so popular!

58
00:05:18,860 --> 00:05:20,570
Go and have fun on your own.

59
00:05:21,070 --> 00:05:22,822
What kind of idea is that?

60
00:05:24,324 --> 00:05:29,037
Let's play Yamanote Line game
at Satoru Gojo's favorite location!

61
00:05:29,620 --> 00:05:31,039
All

62
00:05:32,081 --> 00:05:34,500
Please keep it up.

63
00:05:34,584 --> 00:05:39,047
Itadori needs your stupidity now.

64
00:05:40,757 --> 00:05:43,593
I'll let you complete a few big missions.

65
00:05:44,927 --> 00:05:48,848
That wasn't what I meant
when I said "big."

66
00:05:49,432 --> 00:05:50,558
Nanami.

67
00:05:50,641 --> 00:05:53,186
Did you tell Yuji about
the finger in Yoshino's house--

68
00:05:53,269 --> 00:05:54,729
I didn't tell him.

69
00:05:54,812 --> 00:05:58,149
He will probably
blame himself unnecessarily.

70
00:05:58,816 --> 00:06:00,860
I'm glad I left this up to you.

71
00:06:00,943 --> 00:06:02,653
So where's the finger?

72
00:06:03,946 --> 00:06:06,324
I've handed it over to the superiors.

73
00:06:06,407 --> 00:06:09,952
If I give it to you,
you'll let Itadori eat it, right?

74
00:06:10,578 --> 00:06:14,665
But are you really letting him
return to the team?

75
00:06:15,166 --> 00:06:17,877
If you announce it at the Goodwill Event,

76
00:06:17,960 --> 00:06:20,379
he'll be targeted by the higher-ups again.

77
00:06:20,463 --> 00:06:23,174
Even so, I believe Yuji will be fine.

78
00:06:23,257 --> 00:06:26,052
You should know it well.

79
00:06:27,053 --> 00:06:28,346
What?

80
00:06:28,429 --> 00:06:30,056
Mr. Gojo!

81
00:06:31,724 --> 00:06:33,476
Nanami is here too.

82
00:06:33,559 --> 00:06:34,477
Hey!

83
00:06:34,560 --> 00:06:36,979
Let's go meet them now.

84
00:06:37,063 --> 00:06:38,523
I'm excited!

85
00:06:38,606 --> 00:06:39,774
I'm excited!

86
00:06:39,857 --> 00:06:42,026
I'm excited!

87
00:06:42,110 --> 00:06:43,194
Yuji.

88
00:06:43,277 --> 00:06:44,403
Don't tell me that

89
00:06:44,487 --> 00:06:47,657
you've been hiding for so long,
and now you want to appear normally?

90
00:06:47,740 --> 00:06:49,200
Can't I?

91
00:06:49,992 --> 00:06:52,161
For a dead friend
to reappear after two months

92
00:06:52,245 --> 00:06:54,038
saying they were alive…

93
00:06:54,122 --> 00:06:56,290
Even Jujutsu Sorcerers
don't get that often.

94
00:06:56,374 --> 00:06:58,251
You should give them a surprise.

95
00:07:00,711 --> 00:07:02,588
In short, just leave it to me.

96
00:07:02,672 --> 00:07:03,631
What?

97
00:07:06,634 --> 00:07:09,720
The first-year students will be
shocked, happy, crying, and laughing.

98
00:07:09,804 --> 00:07:12,223
The second-year
and Kyoto's students will cry as well.

99
00:07:12,306 --> 00:07:15,268
Some will cry until they vomit!

100
00:07:16,352 --> 00:07:19,689
They will cry so much that
even global warming will be resolved!

101
00:07:22,692 --> 00:07:23,943
Nice!

102
00:07:24,026 --> 00:07:25,278
What should I do?

103
00:07:25,361 --> 00:07:27,447
Mr. Gojo, what should I do?

104
00:07:27,530 --> 00:07:29,073
You don't have to do anything.

105
00:07:29,157 --> 00:07:30,950
Just do as I say.

106
00:07:31,033 --> 00:07:32,535
Just go along with my plan.

107
00:07:32,618 --> 00:07:34,454
So what should I do to follow your plan?

108
00:07:34,537 --> 00:07:37,707
-You being alive is already a surprise.
-Just flow along with me.

109
00:07:37,790 --> 00:07:38,916
Why…

110
00:07:39,500 --> 00:07:41,919
Why is everyone all empty-handed?

111
00:07:42,003 --> 00:07:43,087
-What?
-What?

112
00:07:43,171 --> 00:07:45,423
That's our question.
What's with all the luggage?

113
00:07:45,506 --> 00:07:48,426
I mean we're going to Kyoto, right?

114
00:07:48,509 --> 00:07:51,929
The Sister-School Goodwill Event in Kyoto.

115
00:07:52,013 --> 00:07:55,266
It's a Sister-School Goodwill Event
with the Kyoto School…

116
00:07:55,349 --> 00:07:56,309
held in Tokyo.

117
00:07:56,392 --> 00:07:57,435
FAMOUS IN UENO
PANDA

118
00:07:57,518 --> 00:07:59,896
No way!

119
00:07:59,979 --> 00:08:03,065
-No wonder I've always felt weird.
-What am I preparing for?

120
00:08:03,149 --> 00:08:04,859
-Yes.
-Salmon.

121
00:08:04,942 --> 00:08:07,904
-It's held by last year's winner.
-This is too much! It's a fraud!

122
00:08:07,987 --> 00:08:09,947
Don't go winning, idiot!

123
00:08:10,031 --> 00:08:12,241
We didn't compete last year!

124
00:08:12,325 --> 00:08:15,453
Yuta was the only one who joined
last year to make up for the numbers.

125
00:08:15,536 --> 00:08:17,413
That was before Rika was freed.

126
00:08:17,497 --> 00:08:19,540
I heard that he dominated the competition.

127
00:08:19,624 --> 00:08:21,751
But it was held in Kyoto,
so we didn't see it.

128
00:08:22,502 --> 00:08:25,046
I won't forgive you, Yuta Okkotsu!

129
00:08:25,129 --> 00:08:27,632
Although I've never met you before!

130
00:08:27,715 --> 00:08:29,091
That's unjustified resentment.

131
00:08:29,175 --> 00:08:30,426
-Salmon.
-What?

132
00:08:33,513 --> 00:08:36,432
Hey. They are here.

133
00:08:37,266 --> 00:08:38,392
Oh, my.

134
00:08:38,476 --> 00:08:41,562
Everyone from the Tokyo school is here.

135
00:08:43,439 --> 00:08:45,274
Are you here to greet us?

136
00:08:45,983 --> 00:08:47,276
It's really disgusting.

137
00:08:47,360 --> 00:08:49,278
MAI ZENIN
SECOND-YEAR STUDENT

138
00:08:49,362 --> 00:08:51,781
Okkotsu is not here.

139
00:08:51,864 --> 00:08:53,783
AOI TODO
THIRD-YEAR STUDENT

140
00:08:53,866 --> 00:08:56,744
Shut up and give me those boxes of cakes.

141
00:08:56,827 --> 00:08:59,080
Yatsuhashi, kuzukiri,
and buckwheat biscuits, too!

142
00:08:59,163 --> 00:09:00,122
Salmon.

143
00:09:00,206 --> 00:09:01,791
Are you guys hungry?

144
00:09:01,874 --> 00:09:03,834
What's wrong with that first-year student?

145
00:09:03,918 --> 00:09:04,794
It's terrifying.

146
00:09:04,877 --> 00:09:06,796
MOMO NISHIMIYA
THIRD-YEAR STUDENT

147
00:09:06,879 --> 00:09:09,006
It's good that Okkotsu is not here,

148
00:09:09,090 --> 00:09:11,133
but two first-years
is too much of a handicap.

149
00:09:11,217 --> 00:09:12,301
It's a robot!

150
00:09:12,385 --> 00:09:14,303
ULTIMATE MECHAMARU
SECOND-YEAR STUDENT

151
00:09:14,387 --> 00:09:17,306
A Jujutsu Sorcerer's strength
has nothing to do with age.

152
00:09:17,390 --> 00:09:19,308
NORITOSHI KAMO
THIRD-YEAR STUDENT

153
00:09:19,392 --> 00:09:21,310
Especially Fushiguro.

154
00:09:21,894 --> 00:09:24,313
He's from the bloodline
of the Zenin Family.

155
00:09:24,397 --> 00:09:26,774
He's much better
than the main family bloodline.

156
00:09:26,857 --> 00:09:27,775
Damn it.

157
00:09:27,858 --> 00:09:28,943
What's wrong?

158
00:09:29,026 --> 00:09:30,027
Nothing.

159
00:09:30,111 --> 00:09:31,237
Hey there, you guys.

160
00:09:31,320 --> 00:09:33,155
You two should calm down.

161
00:09:33,239 --> 00:09:35,157
KASUMI MIWA
SECOND-YEAR STUDENT

162
00:09:35,992 --> 00:09:39,078
Come on. Don't quarrel among ourselves.

163
00:09:39,161 --> 00:09:41,539
You kids…

164
00:09:41,622 --> 00:09:43,541
UTAHIME IORI
SEMI-GRADE 1 JUJUTSU SORCERER

165
00:09:43,624 --> 00:09:46,043
So where's that fool?

166
00:09:46,127 --> 00:09:47,670
Satoru is late.

167
00:09:47,753 --> 00:09:50,464
There's no way a fool
is going to be on time.

168
00:09:50,548 --> 00:09:53,509
Nobody said that fool is Mr. Gojo.

169
00:09:53,593 --> 00:09:54,552
-What?
-What?

170
00:09:57,597 --> 00:09:59,473
Sorry to keep you waiting!

171
00:09:59,557 --> 00:10:00,433
Damn it.

172
00:10:00,516 --> 00:10:01,976
-Satoru Gojo.
-Satoru Gojo!

173
00:10:02,935 --> 00:10:05,313
Hey, everyone's here!

174
00:10:05,396 --> 00:10:08,357
I went on a business trip abroad.

175
00:10:08,441 --> 00:10:10,943
So I brought some souvenirs for everyone.

176
00:10:11,027 --> 00:10:12,361
That's sudden.

177
00:10:12,445 --> 00:10:13,946
Isn't it because of his jet lag?

178
00:10:14,030 --> 00:10:15,948
-Here's for everyone from Kyoto.
-What?

179
00:10:16,032 --> 00:10:17,700
An amulet of a certain tribe.

180
00:10:17,783 --> 00:10:19,035
None for Utahime.

181
00:10:19,118 --> 00:10:20,202
I don't want it!

182
00:10:20,286 --> 00:10:23,331
And this is a local product
for everyone from Tokyo!

183
00:10:25,416 --> 00:10:27,710
Overly-excited adults are creepy.

184
00:10:31,255 --> 00:10:34,216
Yes! OPP!

185
00:10:34,300 --> 00:10:37,011
This is Yuji Itadori,
who was presumed dead!

186
00:10:40,640 --> 00:10:42,016
What?

187
00:10:42,099 --> 00:10:43,142
What?

188
00:10:43,225 --> 00:10:44,518
What?

189
00:10:44,602 --> 00:10:47,480
They don't look happy at all!

190
00:10:48,356 --> 00:10:49,607
No way…

191
00:10:49,690 --> 00:10:51,776
Hello, everyone from Kyoto.

192
00:10:51,859 --> 00:10:55,112
This is Ryomen Sukuna's vessel,
Yuji Itadori.

193
00:10:55,196 --> 00:10:56,489
The Kyoto students…

194
00:10:57,323 --> 00:11:00,076
They are only interested in the dolls!

195
00:11:01,869 --> 00:11:04,205
Sukuna's vessel?

196
00:11:04,288 --> 00:11:06,499
What's going on?

197
00:11:06,582 --> 00:11:08,501
YOSHINOBU GAKUGANJI
PRINCIPAL

198
00:11:08,584 --> 00:11:09,502
What?

199
00:11:09,585 --> 00:11:11,504
Principal Gakuganji!

200
00:11:11,587 --> 00:11:14,507
My, I'm so glad!

201
00:11:14,590 --> 00:11:19,845
I was worried that
you were going to die from shock.

202
00:11:21,097 --> 00:11:23,015
Curse you, brat!

203
00:11:28,562 --> 00:11:29,397
Hey.

204
00:11:29,480 --> 00:11:30,773
Yes?

205
00:11:30,856 --> 00:11:32,983
There's something you should say, right?

206
00:11:33,067 --> 00:11:33,901
What?

207
00:11:37,988 --> 00:11:43,077
I'm sorry for not telling you
that I'm still alive.

208
00:11:43,160 --> 00:11:45,955
ITADORI JOINS THE FRAY

209
00:11:56,048 --> 00:12:00,010
TOKYO-KYOTO
SISTER-SCHOOL GOODWILL EVENT

210
00:12:00,094 --> 00:12:02,555
The Tokyo-Kyoto
Sister-School Goodwill Event

211
00:12:02,638 --> 00:12:05,349
will be held across two days.

212
00:12:05,433 --> 00:12:08,227
First day, we'll have a team battle.

213
00:12:09,270 --> 00:12:10,980
WACKY SPIRIT BASH RACE

214
00:12:11,063 --> 00:12:14,567
It's the Wacky Spirit Bash Race!

215
00:12:16,569 --> 00:12:18,320
The rules are simple.

216
00:12:18,863 --> 00:12:22,116
The team who eliminates
the Grade 2 Cursed Spirit

217
00:12:22,199 --> 00:12:25,077
released within the school grounds wins!

218
00:12:25,661 --> 00:12:29,206
Grade 3 and below Cursed Spirits
have been released, too.

219
00:12:29,290 --> 00:12:31,834
If there's no winner before sunset,

220
00:12:31,917 --> 00:12:35,463
the winner is decided
by the number of eliminations.

221
00:12:35,546 --> 00:12:37,965
There are no other rules.

222
00:12:38,048 --> 00:12:41,427
You may hinder your opponents in the race,

223
00:12:41,510 --> 00:12:45,514
but don't forget that you are comrades
in the fight against the curses.

224
00:12:45,598 --> 00:12:48,601
The Goodwill Event
is for you to understand

225
00:12:48,684 --> 00:12:50,978
your comrades and yourself
in the competition.

226
00:12:51,687 --> 00:12:53,355
Please don't kill each other.

227
00:12:53,439 --> 00:12:57,568
Don't cause irreparable damage
to your opponent.

228
00:12:59,320 --> 00:13:02,615
All right, you are all dismissed.

229
00:13:02,698 --> 00:13:03,991
The race will begin at noon!

230
00:13:06,869 --> 00:13:08,412
TOKYO SCHOOL TEAM MEETING

231
00:13:08,496 --> 00:13:10,080
Excuse me.

232
00:13:10,164 --> 00:13:13,000
We're comrades.

233
00:13:13,083 --> 00:13:15,920
This kind of bullying
seems a bit excessive.

234
00:13:16,003 --> 00:13:18,130
Shut up.
Keep it like that for the time being.

235
00:13:18,214 --> 00:13:19,381
Come on, now.

236
00:13:19,465 --> 00:13:23,135
He has explained the reason.
Just forgive him.

237
00:13:23,219 --> 00:13:24,845
The panda spoke!

238
00:13:24,929 --> 00:13:26,430
Salmon.

239
00:13:26,514 --> 00:13:27,806
What?

240
00:13:27,890 --> 00:13:30,434
Inumaki is
a Cursed Speech Jujutsu Sorcerer.

241
00:13:30,518 --> 00:13:34,271
His cursed technique enhances and
forcefully activates the effects of words.

242
00:13:34,355 --> 00:13:37,358
He limits his vocabulary
for safety purposes.

243
00:13:37,441 --> 00:13:40,277
If you tell someone to die,
will that person really die?

244
00:13:40,361 --> 00:13:41,570
Impressive.

245
00:13:41,654 --> 00:13:43,989
It's not as convenient as you think.

246
00:13:44,073 --> 00:13:47,034
It depends on
the strength of the sorcerer.

247
00:13:47,117 --> 00:13:50,412
Using strong vocabulary
will get a strong rebound,

248
00:13:50,496 --> 00:13:52,831
and it rebounds to himself at worst.

249
00:13:53,332 --> 00:13:57,086
So the vocabulary restriction
is also to protect himself.

250
00:13:57,169 --> 00:13:58,504
I see.

251
00:13:58,587 --> 00:14:01,298
So why can you talk?

252
00:14:01,382 --> 00:14:02,716
Are you a new breed of panda?

253
00:14:02,800 --> 00:14:05,135
How could he reveal
someone else's cursed technique?

254
00:14:05,219 --> 00:14:06,220
It's okay.

255
00:14:06,303 --> 00:14:08,472
It won't matter
if Toge's technique is revealed.

256
00:14:08,973 --> 00:14:11,600
-Anyway, Yuji…
-What?

257
00:14:11,684 --> 00:14:13,602
Give me back the Slaughter Demon.

258
00:14:14,353 --> 00:14:15,896
Satoru lent it to you, right?

259
00:14:17,898 --> 00:14:19,942
Well…

260
00:14:21,944 --> 00:14:23,279
Lend me.

261
00:14:23,779 --> 00:14:24,989
Here you go.

262
00:14:26,615 --> 00:14:28,534
I broke it.

263
00:14:28,617 --> 00:14:30,244
Give it back.

264
00:14:32,413 --> 00:14:35,749
It's with Mr. Gojo.

265
00:14:35,833 --> 00:14:38,419
That stupid blindfolded man!

266
00:14:38,502 --> 00:14:39,837
Really?

267
00:14:43,257 --> 00:14:44,258
That's disgusting.

268
00:14:44,341 --> 00:14:46,552
So what's the plan?

269
00:14:46,635 --> 00:14:49,763
We expected a team battle,

270
00:14:49,847 --> 00:14:51,682
but our members have increased.

271
00:14:51,765 --> 00:14:53,976
Changing our battle strategy?
There's no time.

272
00:14:54,059 --> 00:14:55,185
Bonito flakes.

273
00:14:55,269 --> 00:14:58,188
That depends on Yuji. What can you do?

274
00:14:58,689 --> 00:15:00,024
I can punch and kick.

275
00:15:00,107 --> 00:15:03,986
-There are enough people who can do that.
-What?

276
00:15:04,945 --> 00:15:08,532
I don't know what this guy
did while he was dead,

277
00:15:09,116 --> 00:15:10,868
but if Tokyo and Kyoto School students

278
00:15:10,951 --> 00:15:13,662
fight without cursed energy…

279
00:15:14,246 --> 00:15:16,206
Itadori will win.

280
00:15:16,290 --> 00:15:17,750
Wow.

281
00:15:18,751 --> 00:15:21,545
Megumi has fought Aoi before,

282
00:15:22,338 --> 00:15:24,173
so he's credible.

283
00:15:24,757 --> 00:15:26,383
Interesting.

284
00:15:30,054 --> 00:15:31,221
KYOTO SCHOOL TEAM MEETING

285
00:15:31,305 --> 00:15:33,432
Sukuna's vessel…

286
00:15:33,933 --> 00:15:36,769
Kill Yuji Itadori.

287
00:15:36,852 --> 00:15:38,854
That is not a human.

288
00:15:38,938 --> 00:15:41,190
You can do whatever.

289
00:15:41,273 --> 00:15:43,150
I'll treat it as an accident.

290
00:15:43,233 --> 00:15:45,861
No need to worry or hesitate.

291
00:15:45,945 --> 00:15:47,863
How unpleasant.

292
00:15:47,947 --> 00:15:49,949
Regardless of whether
we can kill him or not,

293
00:15:50,032 --> 00:15:52,868
he's here because he can't die, right?

294
00:15:52,952 --> 00:15:56,872
I heard that he committed suicide.

295
00:15:56,956 --> 00:16:01,835
What do you need to pay attention to
when killing a Jujutsu Sorcerer?

296
00:16:01,919 --> 00:16:02,962
Kamo.

297
00:16:03,045 --> 00:16:03,879
Yes.

298
00:16:04,463 --> 00:16:07,299
To prevent Jujutsu Sorcerers
from becoming curses after death,

299
00:16:07,383 --> 00:16:08,884
we kill them with cursed energy.

300
00:16:08,968 --> 00:16:10,344
That's right.

301
00:16:10,427 --> 00:16:14,932
There will be no problem
if you kill him with cursed energy.

302
00:16:15,015 --> 00:16:18,894
Now Yuji Itadori
has control over the body.

303
00:16:18,978 --> 00:16:22,272
As long as Sukuna doesn't appear,
he's just a normal first-year student.

304
00:16:22,356 --> 00:16:23,857
It's easy to kill--

305
00:16:25,442 --> 00:16:27,528
Lame. Do as you like.

306
00:16:27,611 --> 00:16:29,029
Todo, come back.

307
00:16:29,738 --> 00:16:32,032
The principal is not finished yet.

308
00:16:32,116 --> 00:16:36,704
Takada will make a guest appearance
on the 11:00 a.m. walking show.

309
00:16:36,787 --> 00:16:39,039
Do I need to explain further?

310
00:16:39,123 --> 00:16:41,917
Just record the show. Come back.

311
00:16:42,001 --> 00:16:45,045
I want to watch both the premiere
and the recording!

312
00:16:45,546 --> 00:16:47,297
Are you looking down on me?

313
00:16:49,633 --> 00:16:50,884
That's not the point.

314
00:16:50,968 --> 00:16:52,678
Listen carefully.

315
00:16:52,761 --> 00:16:54,596
You too, old man!

316
00:16:54,680 --> 00:16:59,601
I've long been disappointed
in everyone's poor taste in women.

317
00:16:59,685 --> 00:17:02,604
Just use whatever strategy you want.

318
00:17:02,688 --> 00:17:06,108
However, try giving me another order…

319
00:17:06,191 --> 00:17:07,693
I'll kill you.

320
00:17:11,822 --> 00:17:13,323
What should we do?

321
00:17:13,407 --> 00:17:17,327
It seems that he's not going to
participate in our battle strategy.

322
00:17:17,411 --> 00:17:19,705
The principal is gone too.

323
00:17:19,788 --> 00:17:22,791
To be honest,
I don't want to be killed by him.

324
00:17:22,875 --> 00:17:24,835
It should be okay.

325
00:17:24,918 --> 00:17:28,714
That guy's going to fight
the Tokyo guys either way.

326
00:17:28,797 --> 00:17:30,883
Since he wants to go rampant,

327
00:17:30,966 --> 00:17:33,761
we just need to focus on the game.

328
00:17:33,844 --> 00:17:37,723
But we have to kill Yuji Itadori.

329
00:17:37,806 --> 00:17:39,475
Are we really killing him?

330
00:17:39,975 --> 00:17:43,353
I don't think he's going to kill him.

331
00:17:43,437 --> 00:17:45,189
Although it looks like he might.

332
00:17:45,272 --> 00:17:47,900
Then we have to keep an eye on Todo,

333
00:17:47,983 --> 00:17:51,779
and deal a fatal blow to Yuji Itadori.

334
00:17:51,862 --> 00:17:53,572
I don't want to do it.

335
00:17:54,198 --> 00:17:57,242
Since we have to deal
with Cursed Spirits too,

336
00:17:57,326 --> 00:17:58,994
I think two on one is just right.

337
00:17:59,495 --> 00:18:00,621
No.

338
00:18:00,704 --> 00:18:03,582
Among the Jujutsu Sorcerers
of Jujutsu High School,

339
00:18:03,665 --> 00:18:07,211
the appearance of a half-baked person
like Yuji Itadori is extremely serious.

340
00:18:07,711 --> 00:18:09,630
Regardless of the Goodwill Event,

341
00:18:10,214 --> 00:18:12,758
I can't turn a blind eye
as a member of Kamo Family.

342
00:18:13,717 --> 00:18:17,971
Everyone from Kyoto School
will attack Yuji Itadori.

343
00:18:18,597 --> 00:18:19,598
Wait a minute.

344
00:18:19,681 --> 00:18:23,560
What if Itadori and Inumaki are together?

345
00:18:24,144 --> 00:18:26,814
It's too risky for us
since his Cursed Speech

346
00:18:26,897 --> 00:18:28,482
can take us all out at once.

347
00:18:28,565 --> 00:18:31,443
At worst, we might get wiped out.

348
00:18:32,152 --> 00:18:34,071
She's right.

349
00:18:34,571 --> 00:18:39,076
No, it's not that scary
since we know his technique.

350
00:18:39,159 --> 00:18:41,286
I'll take care of Maki.

351
00:18:41,370 --> 00:18:43,580
Give me that brown-haired
first-year student too.

352
00:18:43,664 --> 00:18:45,165
Listen to what you say.

353
00:18:45,249 --> 00:18:47,167
You're acting like Todo.

354
00:18:49,837 --> 00:18:52,464
So what do you want to talk about?

355
00:18:53,048 --> 00:18:54,883
What? Why are you angry?

356
00:18:55,467 --> 00:18:57,386
I'm not angry.

357
00:18:57,469 --> 00:19:00,931
That's right. I didn't do anything.

358
00:19:01,974 --> 00:19:04,059
Someone in Jujutsu High School…

359
00:19:04,643 --> 00:19:07,396
is colluding with
Cursed Users or Cursed Spirits.

360
00:19:08,397 --> 00:19:09,731
Impossible!

361
00:19:09,815 --> 00:19:12,192
I can understand Cursed Users,
but Cursed Spirits?

362
00:19:12,276 --> 00:19:16,238
Recently, Cursed Spirits
of that level keep emerging.

363
00:19:16,321 --> 00:19:20,284
They not only understand words,
but can even act in a group.

364
00:19:20,367 --> 00:19:21,994
That person may think

365
00:19:22,077 --> 00:19:24,329
they are just colluding with Cursed Users.

366
00:19:24,955 --> 00:19:28,292
So I want you to help me
investigate the Kyoto campus.

367
00:19:29,376 --> 00:19:32,296
What if I'm the mole?

368
00:19:32,379 --> 00:19:33,797
That's impossible.

369
00:19:33,881 --> 00:19:36,425
You're weak, and you don't have the guts--

370
00:19:38,969 --> 00:19:40,220
You're terrifying.

371
00:19:40,304 --> 00:19:44,391
-No man likes a fierce woman!
-I'm your senior!

372
00:19:48,937 --> 00:19:49,897
Itadori.

373
00:19:49,980 --> 00:19:50,814
What?

374
00:19:51,398 --> 00:19:52,441
Are you okay?

375
00:19:52,524 --> 00:19:53,400
Yes.

376
00:19:53,483 --> 00:19:56,236
Seems like I've got a big role,
but there'll always be a way.

377
00:19:56,320 --> 00:19:57,905
I'm not talking about that.

378
00:19:57,988 --> 00:19:59,239
Something happened, right?

379
00:19:59,990 --> 00:20:01,241
Nothing happened.

380
00:20:04,536 --> 00:20:05,746
Something did happen.

381
00:20:07,289 --> 00:20:10,459
But I'm really fine.

382
00:20:11,335 --> 00:20:15,214
In fact, I don't want to lose
because of that.

383
00:20:16,340 --> 00:20:17,716
Good.

384
00:20:18,300 --> 00:20:21,136
I kind of don't want to lose, either.

385
00:20:21,220 --> 00:20:23,013
What do you mean "kind of"?

386
00:20:23,096 --> 00:20:25,057
You were knocked out before.

387
00:20:25,140 --> 00:20:27,768
It will be a complete victory!
Let's beat them up!

388
00:20:27,851 --> 00:20:29,228
For Maki's sake, too!

389
00:20:29,311 --> 00:20:30,687
Don't say that.

390
00:20:30,771 --> 00:20:32,022
Spicy cod roe!

391
00:20:32,105 --> 00:20:34,233
Yes, for the sake of Maki!

392
00:20:34,316 --> 00:20:36,068
I said, stop it!

393
00:20:38,445 --> 00:20:39,780
Well then…

394
00:20:40,405 --> 00:20:41,740
To victory!

395
00:20:43,033 --> 00:20:44,868
Why are you taking charge?

396
00:20:44,952 --> 00:20:45,953
What?

397
00:22:16,752 --> 00:22:18,503
Juju Stroll!

398
00:22:18,587 --> 00:22:21,548
SUSHI EISHU

399
00:22:22,090 --> 00:22:23,050
All right!

400
00:22:23,133 --> 00:22:27,554
Today, we're here at Sushi Eishu.

401
00:22:27,637 --> 00:22:30,140
Why don't you try acting like her?

402
00:22:30,223 --> 00:22:33,018
I would, but you would scold me!

403
00:22:34,519 --> 00:22:36,021
Welcome.

404
00:22:48,617 --> 00:22:51,369
What do you like, Takada?

405
00:22:51,453 --> 00:22:53,163
I like blood clams.

406
00:22:53,246 --> 00:22:56,583
It's a perfect match
with room temperature sake!

407
00:22:56,666 --> 00:22:57,709
How old are you again?

408
00:22:57,793 --> 00:22:58,835
What did you say?

409
00:23:02,881 --> 00:23:05,467
How many years
have you been in this business?

410
00:23:05,967 --> 00:23:07,844
I started when I was 20 years old.

411
00:23:07,928 --> 00:23:09,596
Let me count.

412
00:23:09,679 --> 00:23:12,349
Did you start the business 300 years ago?

413
00:23:12,432 --> 00:23:13,809
Are you drunk?

414
00:23:14,392 --> 00:23:16,812
Thank you for waiting.
Here's your blood clam sushi.

415
00:23:21,358 --> 00:23:22,984
It's delicious!

416
00:23:23,068 --> 00:23:24,778
Can I have yours?

417
00:23:24,861 --> 00:23:26,321
Of course not.

418
00:23:28,615 --> 00:23:31,576
-I'm sorry.
-What are you thinking?

419
00:23:31,660 --> 00:23:34,162
-It looks really delicious.
-It's not bad.

420
00:23:34,246 --> 00:23:36,331
-As expected of Takada.
-This is fun!

421
00:23:36,998 --> 00:23:39,459
Mr. Gojo, do you know what OPP means?

422
00:23:39,543 --> 00:23:41,545
What? It has a meaning?

423
00:23:41,628 --> 00:23:45,382
-It stands for "Ocean Pacific Peace."
-Are you serious?
